  "slug": "outage-report-intake-form",
  "title": "Outage Report Intake Form",
  "subtitle": "An original outage report workflow that turns an initial request into a triaged, evidence-backed assignment, with explicit qualified-review, stop-work, escalation, and accountable handoff controls.",
  "description": "A workflow-complete outage report intake form for the utility interruption and restoration event that captures exact identity, domain observations, supporting evidence, decisions, exceptions, responsible owners, and closeout without replacing professional judgment or the organization's controlling procedures.",
  "use_case": "Use when a coordinator receives a new request and must verify identity, scope, evidence, hazards, feasibility, and the next accountable handoff before field activity is scheduled. The outage coordination lead owns routing, and closure requires documented evidence, disposition of restrictions, and acceptance by the designated reviewer.",
  "risk_tier": "B",
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "intake_routing",
      "title": "Outage report intake identity and routing",
      "guidance": "Create one traceable intake record and assign a person responsible for triage.",
